<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/072A">Exercise <span data-tag="072A">9.7.7.16</span>.</a> In the situation of Proposition <a data-tag="0728" href="/tag/0728">9.7.7.14</a>, suppose that we are given a smaller collection of simplicial sets $\mathbb {K}_0 \subseteq \mathbb {K}$. Show that the relative cocompletion functor </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{ \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \lambda }^{ \mathbb {K}_0-\mathrm{ccomp} }} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{ \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \lambda }^{ \mathbb {K}-\mathrm{ccomp} }} \quad \quad \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\mapsto \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \]
</div>
<p> of Corollary <a data-tag="0703" href="/tag/0703">9.7.1.22</a> can be upgraded to a monoidal functor (see Definition <a data-tag="00DY" href="/tag/00DY">2.1.6.1</a>), with tensor constraints given by the equivalences </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \widehat{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \simeq \widehat{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K}_0} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \]
</div>
<p> supplied by Proposition <a data-tag="0716" href="/tag/0716">9.7.5.3</a>. </p>
</article>
